The Swedes broke into Norway on the evening of 29 October. At the head of some 900 dragoons, Colonel  rode across the Foss Bridge by Kornsjø to clear the way for the infantry of the first column into . Charles XII intended to accompany him, but was persuaded by Stenflycht to stay behind. Stenflycht achieved his objective as the Norwegians positioned to halt his advance retreated towards Fredrikshald.
